d document), under the About Applicant section, there are usually statements such as \\u201cApplicant is the proprietor of the firm M/S Om Construction,\\u201d though the wording may vary in different cases.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Employer_Designation\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants section, the values will typically appear as descriptive statements about the applicant \\u2014 for example, \\u201cApplicant is the proprietor of M/S Om Construction,\\u201d or other similar narrative statements.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Months_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under sections such as About Applicant, About Employment, or Applicant Personal Details\\u2014or any similar sections\\u2014there will typically be explicit mentions of the applicant\\u2019s work experience in the form of months, years, or sometimes specific dates. If a date is provided, the corresponding years and months must be calculated up to the current date.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Years_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under sections such as About Applicant, About Employment, or Applicant Personal Details\\u2014or any similar sections\\u2014there will typically be explicit mentions of the applicant\\u2019s work experience in the form of months, years, or sometimes specific dates. If a date is provided, the corresponding years must be calculated up to the current date and if months are provided then the given months must be converted into an equivalent year count.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Mode_Of_Salary\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the \\\"About Employment\\\" section or similar areas, look for keywords like \\\"having cash salary\\\" or comparable phrases/statements. Analyze these to determine whether the salary mode is cash or bank deposit.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Office_SetUp\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the Income Details section, the field \\u201cBusiness Setup Details\\u201d typically contains values such as Resi-cum-Office Setup or Permanent Structure or other similar relevant descriptions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Lender_PD_Status\",\n    \"description\": \"consider it as Positive if anywhere in the document, Credit manager is mentioned if it is not mentioned then discuss what to be done.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Marital_Status\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants section, you will typically find statements such as \\u201cApplicant is married and residing in a rented house at H No. E7/112, Arera Colony, Bhopal.\\u201d These statements may appear in different wording or under differently named sections. From such sentences, marital status\\u2014such as Married, Single, or other applicable statuses\\u2014can be extracted.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Level_Of_Studies\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants section, the information is usually presented in sentence form\\u2014for example: \\u201cApplicant Mr. Kanhaiya Bharti is about 49 years of age and is a BA graduate by qualification.\\u201d Similar narrative statements may appear, from which the applicant\\u2019s qualification can be extracted.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Number_Of_Dependents\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants section, details about the applicant are usually written in descriptive sentence form. These narratives may also include information about the applicant\\u2019s dependents, from which the number of dependents can be identified if mentioned.If dependent members are mentioned, use the stated number; if none are indicated, record the value as 0.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Current_Residence\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants s