alue from the field \\u201cTenure (Months).\\u201d\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Sanction_Interest_Rate\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Basic Input sheet under the \\u201cProposed Loan Break-up\\u201d section, extract the value from the field \\u201cProposed ROI.\\u201d This value is typically presented in formats like 10.50% or 12.00% etc.\\n\\nWhile extracting the value, do not include the percentage (%) sign. Remove the % symbol and return only the numeric value.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 10.50%\\nOutput: 10.50\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Loan_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM Excel file, within the Basic Input sheet under the Proposed Loan Breakup section, there is a field called \\u201cType of Loan.\\u201d This field typically contains values such as Home Loan.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Type_Of_Employment_Loan\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM Excel file, under the Basic Input sheet, the field \\u201cCustomer Type\\u201d typically contains values such as Salaried, Self-Employed Non-Professional, and similar categories. This field can be found at the top.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Foir\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the AffordableCMAssessedIncome sheet, the field \\u201cFOIR for Applied Loan Amount\\u201d typically contains values such as 44.55%, 33.24%, and similar percentages.\\n\\nWhile extracting the value, do not include the percentage (%) sign. Remove the % symbol and return only the numeric value.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 10.50%\\nOutput: 10.50\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_First_Name\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Basic Input sheet and the Parties to the Loan section, the field \\u201cName\\u201d typically contains values such as Vikram Singh, Girish Kumar Nanda, Mohd. Azhar, and similar entries.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_Surname\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Basic Input sheet and the Parties to the Loan section, the field \\u201cName\\u201d typically contains values such as Vikram Singh, Girish Kumar Nanda, Mohd. Azhar, and similar entries.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Relationship_Of_Coborrower_To_The_Borrower\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM document, locate the section titled \\u201cParties to the Loan.\\u201d Identify the field \\u201cRelationship with Applicant.\\u201d Extract and return the value exactly as it appears in the document (for example: Mother, Spouse, Father, Wife, etc.) without any modification, normalization, or interpretation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Years_In_Current_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the ApplicantSalary sheet, the field \\u201cDate of Joining\\u201d typically contains values such as 19/12/1981, etc.\\nCheck the Date of Joining and calculate the duration up to the current date, then update the corresponding months and years accordingly.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Months_In_Current_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the ApplicantSalary sheet, the field \\u201cDate of Joining\\u201d typically contains values such as 19/12/1981, etc.\\nCheck the Date of Joining and calculate the duration up to the current date, then update the corresponding months and years accordingly.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Mode_Of_Salary\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the sheet -  ApplicantSalary , the field \\u201cRemarks, If any\\u201d typically contains entries such as \\u201cSalary reflected to bank, SALARY NOT REFLECT IN BANKING\\u201d or similar comments. Extract and return the value exactly as it appears in the document without any modification, normalization, or interpretation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Office_SetUp\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the AffordableCMAssessedIncome sheet, the field \\u201cBusiness Setup Details\\u201d typically includes values such as Permanent Structure, Resi-cum-Office Setup, and other similar descriptions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Date_Of_Filing_LatestYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet, the field \\u201cITR Acknowledgement Date\\u201d appears across three assessment years\\u2014such as 2023\\u20132024, 2022\\u20132023, and 2021\\u20132022. For this field, the acknowledgment date must be extracted from the latest assessment year\\u2019s column. Typical values for this field include dates like 29-Jul-2023, 19-Jul-1994, and similar formats.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Financial_Status_LatestYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet, the field \\u201cPAT (Rs)\\u201d appears across three assessment years\\u2014such as 2023\\u20132024, 2022\\u20132023, and 2021\\u20132022. For this field, use the PAT value from the latest assessment year\\u2019s column and apply the following logic:\\n\\nIf the PAT value is up to 1 crore, mark it as Unaudited.\\n\\nIf the PAT value is greater than 1 crore, mark it as Audited.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Gross_Profit_LatestYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet, the field \\u201cTotal Gross Turnover / Receipts (Rs.)\\u201d appears across three assessment years\\u2014for example, 2023\\u20132024, 2022\\u20132023, and 2021\\u20132022. For this PAS field, use the value listed under the latest assessment year. Typical values for this field may include amounts such as 25,33,780, 45,23,280, 1,00,00,123, and similar figures.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Gross_Profit_PreviousYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet, the field \\u201cTotal Gross Turnover / Receipts (Rs.)\\u201d appears across three assessment years\\u2014for example, 2023\\u20132024, 2022\\u20132023, and 2021\\u20132022. For this PAS field, use the value from the second-latest assessment year. Typical values may include amounts such as 25,33,780, 45,23,280, 1,00,00,123, and similar figures.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Gross_Profit_Previous_To_PreviousYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet, the field \\u201cTotal Gross Turnover / Receipts (Rs.)\\u201d is displayed across three assessment years\\u2014such as 2023\\u20132024, 2022\\u20132023, and 2021\\u20132022. For this PAS field, use the value from the previous-to-previous assessment year. Typical values may include figures like 1,00,00,123 and similar amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Type_Of_Employment_Borrower\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Basic Input sheet, the field \\u201cCustomer Type\\u201d typically contains values such as Self-Employed Non-Professional (SENP), Salaried, Self-Employed Professional, and other similar categories.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Manual_ABB\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Banking\\u2013Non PDF sheet, within the Average (Rs.) section, the field \\u201cAverage\\u201d should be extracted from the Average row value shown under the Average (Rs.) section of all months column.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Amount_Of_Salary_Credit\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Applicant Salary sheet haivng section name  Salary, Bonus / Incentive, Reimbursement, or Other Credits from Employer, there will be a field \\u201cAmount (Rs.)\\u201d typically contains values such as 13,410, 1,00,343, and similar amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Existing_Obligation_Out_AMT\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Existing Loans & Facilities & RTR sheet, the field \\u201cCurrent Outstanding (Rs.)\\u201d typically contains values such as 21,000, 2,00,321, and similar outstanding amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Existing_Obligation_EMI\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Existing Loans & Facilities & RTR sheet, the field \\u201cRunning EMI (Rs.)\\u201d typically contains values such as 12,000, 28,444, and similar EMI amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Account_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Banking \\u2013 Non PDF sheet, the field \\u201cA/C Type\\u201d typically contains values such as Savings, Current, and other similar account types.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"No_Of_Months_Banking_Available\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Banking \\u2013 Non PDF sheet, the field \\u201cMonth\\u201d should be used to determine how many months of data are provided. Count all the months listed\\u2014for example, if data is available for January, February, and March, then the total number of months is 3.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"No_Of_Debit_Entries\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Banking \\u2013 Non PDF sheet in the No. of Debit Entries section, the field \\u201cTotal\\u201d typically contains values such as 119, 400, 220, 101, and similar counts. The value shown in front of \\u201cTotal\\u201d within this section should be taken as the extracted value.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Obligation_Status\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Existing Loans & Facilities & RTR sheet, the field \\u201cStatus\\u201d typically contains values such as Active, Closed, To be closed before our disbursal, and other similar status descriptions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Office_Ownership\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the AffordableCMAssessedIncome sheet, the field \\u201cBusiness Premises Ownership\\u201d typically contains values such as Self-Owned, Shared, Rented, and other similar ownership types.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Basic_Salary\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Applicant Salary sheet in the Component section, the field \\u201cBasic\\u201d typically contains numeric values such as 23,000, 12,444, and similar salary component amounts.\"\n  },\