nt Salary sheet in the Component section, the field \\u201cPension\\u201d typically contains values such as 12,000, 45,444, and similar pension amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"PF\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the  Applicant Salary sheet, the field \\u201cPF\\u201d typically contains values such as 7,000, 3,200, 4,000, and similar provident fund amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Income_Tax\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Applicant Salary sheet, the field \\u201cIncome Tax (TDS)\\u201d typically contains values such as 5,000, 12,750, 8,300, and similar TDS deduction amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Rental_Income_Bank_ITR\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the SelfEmployedEligibility sheet in the Other Income section, the field \\u201cRental Income\\u201d typically contains values such as 24,000, 6,000, and other similar rental income amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Rental_Income_Cash\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the SelfEmployedEligibility sheet in the Other Income section, the field \\u201cRental Income (Unregistered)\\u201d typically contains values such as 10,000, 18,500, 5,000, and other similar unregistered rental income amounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"TaxPaid_LatestYear\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the 44AD, 44ADA, 44AE Income sheet in the Particulars section, the field \\u201cTax Paid (Rs.)\\u201d displays values across three assessment years, such as 2023\\u201324, 2022\\u201323, and 2021\\u201322. For this field, the value corresponding to the latest assessment year should be extracted.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Rental_Income_Source_Cash\",\n    \"description\": \"In the CAM file, under the Self Employed Eligibility sheet, the field \\u201cRental Income (Unregistered)\\u201d typically contains values such as 12,000, 8,000, 9,000, and other similar unregistered rental income amounts.\"\n  },\