 under the About Applicant section, there are usually statements such as \\u201cApplicant is the proprietor of the firm M/S Om Construction,\\u201d though the wording may vary in different cases.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Employer_Designation\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicants section, the values will typically appear as descriptive statements about the applicant \\u2014 for example, \\u201cApplicant is the proprietor of M/S Om Construction,\\u201d or other similar narrative statements.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Months_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under sections such as About Applicant, About Employment, or Applicant Personal Details\\u2014or any similar sections\\u2014there will typically be explicit mentions of the applicant\\u2019s work experience in the form of months, years, or sometimes specific dates. If a date is provided, the corresponding years and months must be calculated up to the current date.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Years_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under sections such as About Applicant, About Employment, or Applicant Personal Details\\u2014or any similar sections\\u2014there will typically be explicit mentions of the applicant\\u2019s work experience in the form of months, years, or sometimes specific dates. If a date is provided, the corresponding years must be calculated up to the current date and if months are provided then the given months must be converted into an equivalent year count.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Mode_Of_Salary\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the \\\"About Employment\\\" section or similar areas, look for keywords like \\\"having cash salary\\\" or comparable phrases/statements. Analyze these to determine whether the salary mode is cash or bank deposit.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Office_SetUp\",\n    \"description\":