ourcing_City_Name\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, the city can be found under the Sourcing Channel Details section in the field \\u201cLocation Name.\\u201d Typical entries include cities such as Indore, Lucknow, Mumbai, Noida, Kanpur, Ahmedabad, etc.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Branch_Name\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, the branch-related city information appears under the Sourcing Channel Details section in the field \\u201cLocation Name.\\u201d Common examples include: Indore, Lucknow, Mumbai, Noida, Kanpur, Ahmedabad, etc.\\nThe branch name can be mapped based on this city value.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Sourcing_Channel\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, check the SOURCING CHANNEL DETAILS section under the field \\u201cChannel Name.\\u201d Update the PAS Field only if this value is present; otherwise, mark it as NA.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Final_Sanctioned_Amount\",\n    \"description\": \"Under the Loan Details section, refer to the field \\u201cLoan Amount Requested.\\u201d Use the given value for mapping this PAS Field.\\n\\nConvert the extracted value into a pure numeric amount only, ensuring that all currency symbols and textual units such as Rs, INR, lakh, lacs, crore, etc. are removed. The final output must contain only digits, with no commas, spaces, or special characters (for example, Rs 30 lacs should be returned as 3000000).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Sanction_Loan_Period\",\n    \"description\": \"Under the Loan Details section, use the value from the field \\u201cLoan Tenure (Months)\\u201d for mapping this PAS Field.\\n\\nThis field may contain values such as 240 Months, 240, 198 months, or similar formats.\\nWhile extracting the value, return only the numeric digits. Do not include any text such as \\u201cMonths\\u201d or \\u201cmonths\\u201d in the final output.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 198 months\\nOutput: 198\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Loan_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, at the beginning of the document, there is a section titled Loan Details. Under this section, you will find a field named \\u201cScheme,\\u201d which typically contains values such as PLOT AND  HOME CONSTRUCTION LOAN,  PLOT HOME CONSTRUCTION LOAN among others.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_First_Name\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cName\\u201d will contain values such as Vikram Singh, Girish Kumar Nanda, Mohd. Azhar, and similar applicant names.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_Surname\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cName\\u201d will contain values such as Vikram Singh, Girish Kumar Nanda, Mohd. Azhar, and similar applicant names.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Date_Of_Birth_Of_The_Borrower\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cDate of Birth\\u201d usually values appears in the DD/MM/YYYY format, with sample values such as 02/01/2024, 24/03/1991, and similar dates.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_Address1\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Current/Communication Address section, the fields Address 1, Address 2, and Address 3 typically contain address details such as Ashoka Society, Arera Colony, H. No. E7/112, Bhopal, or similar address information.\\n\\nWhile extracting the address, do not include commas (,) in the final output. If commas appear in the source value, remove them.\\n\\nExample:\\nIf Source: H. No. E7/112, Arera Colony, Bhopal\\nthen Output: H. No. E7/112 Arera Colony Bhopal\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_City\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Current/Communication Address section, the field \\u201cCity\\u201d typically contains values such as Bhopal, Indore, Lucknow, and similar city names.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_PIN\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Current/Communication Address section, the field \\u201cPincode\\u201d typically contains values such as 226024, 110024, 201010, 400503, and similar numeric codes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_MobileNo\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Current/Communication Address section, the field \\u201cMobile No.\\u201d typically contains values such as +91 8377998214, +919876543210, 7823445432, and other similar mobile numbers.\\n\\nWhile extracting the mobile number, do not include the country code (+91). If the country code is present, remove it and return only the 10-digit mobile number.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: +91 8377998214\\nOutput: 8377998214\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Employer_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Occupation/Business Details section, the field \\u201cCompany / Occupation Type\\u201d typically contains values such as Madhya Pradesh Madhyam, Proprietorship, Private limited etc and similar classifications.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Months_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Occupation/Business Details section, the field \\u201cWork Experience / No. of Years in Business\\u201d typically contains values such as 60 months, 80 months, and similar durations.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Years_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Occupation/Business Details section, the field \\u201cWork Experience / No. of Years in Business\\u201d typically contains values such as 60 months, 108 months, and similar durations. If only the total number of years is required, the given months must be converted into an equivalent year count.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Type_Of_Employment_Borrower\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Occupation/Business Details section, the field \\u201cSalaried / Self Employed\\u201d typically contains values such as Salaried, SENP, and other similar classifications.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Borrower_Entity_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"Logic: If the gender is Male or Female, mark the PAS field as Individual.\\nIf the applicant is a Company or any other entity, mark it as Non-Individual.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Gender\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, there is a field labeled \\u201cGender.\\u201d\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Marital_Status\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cMarital Status\\u201d typically contains values such as Married, Single, and similar statuses.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Level_Of_Studies\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cQualification\\u201d typically contains values such as Graduate and other similar educational qualifications.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Current_Residence\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Personal Details section, the field \\u201cCurrent Residence\\u201d typically contains values such as Rented, Owned, Lease House, and other similar residence types.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Employer_Name\",\n    \"description\": \"In the Application Form, under the Occupation/Business Details section, the field \\u201cCompany Name\\u201d typically contains values such as Madhya Pradesh Madhyam, Om Constructions, and other similar organization names.\"\n  }\n]\n\nInstructions:\nFor CAM Some of content is from excel provided as plain text, where each sheet starts with a divider and its name, like:\n============================================================\n[SHEET: SheetName]\n============================================================\nFor each field, extract the value based on its description, searching only within the relevant sheet and its data section.\nIf a field is not found or not applicable in the specified sheet, use null as its value.\nReturn a JSON object with field names as keys and extracted values as values.\n", "response": "{\n  \"Loan_Number\": \"3000023637\",\n  \"Sourcing_Region\": \"Bhopal\",\n  \"Sourcing_City_Name\": \"Bhopal\",\n  \"Branch_Name\": \"Bhopal\",\n  \"Sourcing_Channel\": \"Sohan Singh Lingwal\",\n  \"Final_Sanctioned_Amount\": \"3500000\",\n  \"Sanction_Loan_Period\": \"240\",\n  \"Loan_Type\": \"CONSTRUCTION LOAN\",\n  \"Borrower_First_Name\": \"KANHAIYA\",\n  \"Borrower_Surname\": \"BHARTI\",\n  \"Date_Of_Birth_Of_The_Borrower\": \"02/11/1975\",\n  \"Borrower_Address1\": \"Ashoka society arera Colony H. No. E7/112 Bhopal\",\n  \"Borrower_City\": \"Bhopal\",\n  \"Borrower_PIN\": \"462001\",\n  \"Borrower_MobileNo\": \"9907133611\",\n  \"Employer_Type\": \"Proprietorship\",\n  \"Months_In_Total_Employment\": \"60\",\n  \"Years_In_Total_Employment\": \"5\",\n  \"Type_Of_Employment_Borrower\": \"SENP\",\n  \"Borrower_Entity_Type\": \"Individual\",\n  \"Gender\": \"Male\",\n  \"Marital_Status\": \"Married\",\n  \"Level_Of_Studies\": \"Graduate\",\n  \"Current_Residence\": \"Rented\",\n  \"Employer_Name\": \"OM CONSTRUCTIONS\"\n}"}
