rn only the numeric digits. Do not include any text such as \\u201cMonths\\u201d or \\u201cmonths\\u201d in the final output.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 198 months\\nOutput: 198\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Sanction_Interest_Rate\",\n    \"description\": \"In the \\u201cProposed Loan Break-up\\u201d section which will be tabular form, refer to the field name \\u201cProposed ROI,\\u201d where the value will appear in formats such as 10.50% or 12.00% etc\\n\\nWhile extracting the value, do not include the percentage (%) sign. Remove the % symbol and return only the numeric value.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 10.50%\\nOutput: 10.50\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Loan_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), within the Proposed Loan Breakup table, there is a field  \\u201cType of Loan.\\u201d This field generally includes values such as Home Loan, Composite Loan (Plot Purchase plus Home Construction), and similar options.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Foir\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the Income Details section, which contains tabular data, the field \\u201cFOIR for Applied Loan Amount\\u201d typically includes values such as 55.02%, 33.24%, and similar percentages.\\n\\nWhile extracting the value, do not include the percentage (%) sign. Remove the % symbol and return only the numeric value.\\n\\nExample:\\nSource: 10.50%\\nOutput: 10.50\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Sole_Child\",\n    \"description\": \"Anwhere, If mentioned in PD then make it as Yes, if nothing is mentioned then make it as No\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Employer_Type\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), under the About Applicant section, there are usually statements such as \\u201cApplicant is the proprietor of the firm M/S Om Construction,\\u201d though the wording may vary in different cases.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"field_name\": \"Months_In_Total_Employment\",\n    \"description\": \"In the PD (Word document), und